 helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Interaction_DragView","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Drags a layer in any direction with momentum and rubber-band bounds. The draggable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card responds to touch input via Origami’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"type":"text","text":" patch, which wires its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"output "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"type":"text","text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card snaps back to its resting position."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"Interaction_DragView","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Interaction_DragView","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/fileExporter(isPresented:documents:contentType:onCompletion:)-99oe5":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"fileExporter(isPresented:documents:contentType:onCompletion:)","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/fileexporter(ispresented:documents:contenttype:oncompletion:)-99oe5","abstract":[],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Intera